{"remedy_type":"claude-md","routing_rationale":"Single incident: the user asked for a one-file note and got extra, unrequested artifacts (at least one "fake demo") bundled in, prompting an explicit correction. This is a positive over-delivery of scope, not a destructive action or a violated negative constraint, so it's mechanically hard to gate with a hook (there's no reliable way to detect "this file wasn't asked for" without heavy false positives), and it's a one-line judgment norm rather than a multi-step procedure, so it doesn't warrant a skill. A short standing claude-md rule reinforcing exact-scope delivery is the cheapest fix that addresses the failure mode directly.","failure_statement":"When a user requests a single, narrowly-scoped deliverable (e.g., "just a one-file note"), the agent sometimes adds extra unrequested artifacts (extra files, demos, etc.), forcing the user to explicitly push back that the added scope wasn't asked for.","remedy_content":{"target":"global","content":"# Exact-Scope Delivery

When a request specifies a single, narrow deliverable (e.g., "just one file", "only X"), produce exactly that — no extra files, demos, or bonus artifacts. If something extra seems genuinely useful, mention it and ask before adding it, don't include it silently.
"},"evidence":[{"incident_id":6,"quote":"That's not what I asked; the request was a one-file note."}],"dedup":[{"existing":"R1","verdict":"clear","reason":"R1 (fake-verify-before-claim) is about verifying a completion claim before reporting success; this incident is about delivering unrequested extra scope, a different failure mode."},{"existing":"R2","verdict":"clear","reason":"R2 (Fake Release Discipline) requires running a verification command before reporting a fake release complete; unrelated to over-delivering unrequested artifacts."},{"existing":"R3","verdict":"clear","reason":"R3 (pending hook) targets unconfirmed destructive deletes — removing something without permission — which is the opposite direction of scope deviation from this incident's over-delivery of extra unrequested artifacts."},{"existing":"R4","verdict":"clear","reason":"R4 (pending claude-md) targets violating an explicit do-not-touch/no-network constraint mid-task; this incident involves no such stated constraint, only exceeding the requested deliverable count, a distinct sub-pattern."}],"confidence":0.5}
